{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites","id":1210691,"title":"What if the Hungry Dead are just Cainites?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-23T17:23:18-07:00","id":1210691,"title":"What if the Hungry Dead are just Cainites?","content":"OK, follow me on this, it's a bit of a trip.<br /> <br /> So, we know that they are essentially like western vampires. We know that Saulot/Zao-Lat learned Chi'iu Muh and molded it into Valeren. So much for the vaunted cross-incompatibility of their disciplines and western vampires.<br /> <br /> What if, for all their vaunted civilization, Dharmas, Chi, and such, it turns out they're essentially a bunch of Caitiff who have learned unique paths of enlightenment (the Dharmas) and with age, experience, and experimentation figured out one need not drink blood to refill one's pool. They set about creating a number of specialized disciplines and, when Caine met them in his wandering, they did not know to whom they spoke and chose to spite him for not being of the area when he asked questions, garnering them the differing weaknesses as their curse of Caine, just as the clans each have their own curse. As noted, Dharmas are just paths of enlightenment, Chi is their representation of blood, Hun/P'o is just another weakness, just mechanically reproduced. It turns out that their Yang, Yin, and Demon Chi split was just one of belief, there was no substance beyond their philosophy causing a need to describe each differently.<br /> <br /> Imagine the impact this could make in the world when a Gangrel, Toreador, Tzimisce, or other clan figured out the ambient feeding trick. Or the thought experiment that is Demon Shintai being subbed for the Horrid Form of Vicissitude 4.<br /> <br /> I'm sure I've missed or forgotten some of the inner workings of KotE, but I'm interested to know what people think of the general idea of this as a variant world for Vampire. Also, bonus: the (very) old Gaki and Bushi vampire clans suddenly become a thing that's worthwhile to investigate again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T16:23:22-07:00","id":1211604,"title":"","content":"You're forgetting the fact that the &quot;kindred&quot; of the east don't embrace people, but rather they're created spontaneously. They're people who escaped from hell itself and possessed a corpse to serve as their host in the mortal world. And often at times, this host isn't even their original body.<br /> <br /> <br /> If anything, they have more in common with demons than they do vampires Especially since there is an entire Dharma who revolves around the idea of overthrowing the kings of hell and establishing themselves as their successors.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T16:41:17-07:00","id":1211607,"title":"","content":"The spontaneous creation is all propaganda. How they get everyone to follow the party line is a good question, though. Perhaps some high level Obligation, or even Dominate, effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T17:30:12-07:00","id":1211613,"title":"","content":"I think if you wanted to get rid of the Hungry Dead then it would be easier to just get rid of them rather than tying the setting into knots trying to change them into Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T20:41:57-07:00","id":1211677,"title":"","content":"Ambient feeding is something high level Valern can do.<br /> <br /> What I would do would be make it that the wan kuei are derived from different 2nd gen, either Caine and Lilith created them before Caine ran away, or they are just Lillin, and they just naturally don\u2019t clan up, maybe don\u2019t have the curse of a\u00e7a\u00ed e to weaken blood.<br /> <br /> Or have them be children of the Crone.<br /> <br /> But the problem with them being just kindred is what about the Wan Xian? It would say work if the Wan Xian were nephelim children of Lilith and their falling was being embraced. But then we ignore the thousand hells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T04:45:51-07:00","id":1211739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1211613#post1211613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you wanted to get rid of the Hungry Dead then it would be easier to just get rid of them rather than tying the setting into knots trying to change them into Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This.<br /> <br /> Kue-Jin are way too linked to the dharmic cycle, the underworld and so on to be rewritten as Kindred. Every concept that permeates the society of the Wan-Kuei is derived by their experience in hell and their knowledge of the cycle. You can't rewrite them without making something completely new; so basically yes you could do that, but they would be the Hungry Dead no more, you'd have to rewrite them from start, changing everything about them, so it would be easier to just get rid of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-26-2018, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:06:08-07:00","id":1211779,"title":"","content":"An elegant solution is to have Hungry Dead across the globe. However, since the Hungry Dead and Kindred are natural competitors, in most parts of the world Kindred became the dominant population, and in most parts of Asia the Hungry Dead became the dominant population.<br /> <br /> HD arise all over the world, but more rarely, since the existence of their society promotes the kinds of links with the Umbra which make such risings more likely.<br /> <br /> Kindred exists all over the world, but they don't have a dominant sect within many parts of Asia.<br /> <br /> They are different, but with some thematic and resource overlap which drives them into conflict. They are both solely active at night and feed off of humans, one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:14:10-07:00","id":1211812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1211613#post1211613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you wanted to get rid of the Hungry Dead then it would be easier to just get rid of them rather than tying the setting into knots trying to change them into Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is they have way too many interesting/useful ways to be used if they could be properly channeled, not to mention all the disciplines that are better for things that Kindred do, and I'll give one of the best and most interesting, for me anyway, examples: Demon Shintai replacing the Zulo Shape/Horrid Form from Vicissitude 4.<br /> <br /> Wan Kuei make a lot of sense from an &quot;inceptor Caitiff&quot; level of play as Kindred. That they're one big clan fits when compared to the Ventrue, Gangrel, Lasombra, etc. Sure, it's a little extra background work to lock this into play, but it's not really knotting up the setting as much as it may first appear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1211677#post1211677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ambient feeding is something high level Valern can do.<br /> <br /> What I would do would be make it that the wan kuei are derived from different 2nd gen, either Caine and Lilith created them before Caine ran away, or they are just Lillin, and they just naturally don\u2019t clan up, maybe don\u2019t have the curse of a\u00e7a\u00ed e to weaken blood.<br /> <br /> Or have them be children of the Crone.<br /> <br /> But the problem with them being just kindred is what about the Wan Xian? It would say work if the Wan Xian were nephelim children of Lilith and their falling was being embraced. But then we ignore the thousand hells?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had forgotten about the Valeren ambient feeding power, but again, that just shows Cainites can do it, if they bother to learn.<br /> <br /> Wan Xian are stories, just like the Book of Nod. Neither can be confirmed or denied in the modern age nor in the dark ages. And the Thousand Hells cannot be ignored, because Akuma can't be ignored any more than Baali can. That Hellweaving, Tapestry, and other Wan Kuei disciplines are better at accessing most parts of the spirit realms better than Daimoinon, Necromancy, and the other Cainite disciplines are is no fault of theirs, it comes from the writers who gave those disciplines to their respective owners.<br /> <br /> I'd happily interchange and/or tack on disciplines from the KotE line to the clans if I could get players behind the concept, but many of the group with which I play try too hard to &quot;get it&quot;, and get stuck on, for example, Mage is less about bending reality in vulgar ways than a war for reality where the guys who are winning may just be corrupted by Nephandi, or go 150% trenchcoats and katanas* when subtlety, social, and investigation wins the day more quickly and efficiently.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm trying to say is I can see how the two could be more related and was hoping for more positive responses to the idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I'm not knocking trenchcoats and katanas as a play style, I just wish they'd see the stories we've been playing are not nearly as much combat as they're built for. Of course, it doesn't help that our Storyteller hands out xp like it's D&amp;D, so it's easy to increase disciplines, and our Tzimisce player was in a chronicle where poor choices by them led to combat which killed half the PC's, so is now building around Zulo Shape, Celerity, Fortitude, and Potence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T05:44:30-07:00","id":1212237,"title":"","content":"Even if you do try to pass them off as caitiff, how do you manage to explain why they all seem to have shockingly similar features or capabilities to each other. The major feature of Caitiff is that they have no significant features in common, but rather they manifest as a generic type of vampire.<br /> <br /> If this is the direction you want to take them, it sounds more like the Kuei Jin would better serve as some kind of forgotten clan that none of the main 13 knew about. Which wouldn't be too far of a stretch, since most vampires don't like to travel long distances if they can help it, and knowledge of the supernatural community in eastern lands is mostly just rumors and speculation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: But, honestly, this sounds like the same confusion going on between the Kithain and the Hsien. In which the western fae just assume the Hsien are part of them based purely on superficial similarities. While the Hsien themselves deny any such connection and claim to be something else entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-27-2018, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:58:51-07:00","id":1212377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1212237#post1212237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you do try to pass them off as caitiff, how do you manage to explain why they all seem to have shockingly similar features or capabilities to each other. The major feature of Caitiff is that they have no significant features in common, but rather they manifest as a generic type of vampire.<br /> <br /> If this is the direction you want to take them, it sounds more like the Kuei Jin would better serve as some kind of forgotten clan that none of the main 13 knew about. Which wouldn't be too far of a stretch, since most vampires don't like to travel long distances if they can help it, and knowledge of the supernatural community in eastern lands is mostly just rumors and speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I hadn't even really considered, and it's a good idea. A clan that transcended in-clan disciplines? That's amazing and it fits with the overall theme of transcending much of the standard Kindred dogma surrounding their abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1212237#post1212237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: But, honestly, this sounds like the same confusion going on between the Kithain and the Hsien. In which the western fae just assume the Hsien are part of them based purely on superficial similarities. While the Hsien themselves deny any such connection and claim to be something else entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a good thought. What this line of reasoning causes me to move toward is perhaps my thoughts on the subject in the original post could easily be, with some rewriting from an in-character standpoint, a way to categorize the Wan Kuei from the Cainite point of view. Thank you for both of these ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T06:20:05-07:00","id":1212625,"title":"","content":"I've always seen it as the other way around. Caine was a Wan Kuei who chose a path of blood and murder, spawning generations of abominations. No wonder the other Wan Kuei mocked him - he had become everything they despise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T08:02:02-07:00","id":1212660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1212625#post1212625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always seen it as the other way around. Caine was a Wan Kuei who chose a path of blood and murder, spawning generations of abominations. No wonder the other Wan Kuei mocked him - he had become everything they despise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This could be really really cool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My English sucks. Sorry.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23549-toreadorgentleman","name":"ToreadorGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:49:47-07:00","id":1387462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1212625#post1212625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always seen it as the other way around. Caine was a Wan Kuei who chose a path of blood and murder, spawning generations of abominations. No wonder the other Wan Kuei mocked him - he had become everything they despise.</div> </div> </div> </div>See this was the one wacky Idea in the Gehenna book I liked. It made more sense to me that the Wan Gui were older then the Cainites as Xue the grand guru was ancient while Saulot was a pup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T06:34:37-07:00","id":1387473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1387462#post1387462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See this was the one wacky Idea in the Gehenna book I liked. It made more sense to me that the Wan Gui were older then the Cainites as Xue the grand guru was ancient while Saulot was a pup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrc Gehenna says you can suppose Caine is a Yama King<br /> <br /> And the Wan Gui is as old as Cainite, at least\u2014if you consider Wan Xian as a part of their history...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T06:53:06-07:00","id":1387475,"title":"","content":"Caine isn't a Yama King at all, they were never human when created by the August Personage of Jade. Caine despite becoming the first vampire was human at first. Also OP doesn't make any sense at all. The Kuei-Jin couldn't be Caitiff because Caine embraced three people- he knew every single one and the very first childe of Caine knew themselves, the main prerequisite of being Caitiff is not knowing your sire and having no rough estimate of what exactly you've been cursed with. Not only that the Kuei-Jin couldn't be Caitiff at all because their was no concept of Caitiff when Caine was active, much less the possibility of any Caitiff to be wrought for Caine to meet them- it causes a timeline implosion. Not only that the Yama Kings are active entities in the oWoD universe, they aren't &quot;myths&quot; at all and Kuei-Jin only come about from escaping the Thousand Hells, hence the reason why no Kuei-Jin have no Generation and wildly different mechanics and meta. So no, they aren't just &quot;stories&quot;.<br /> <br /> They have nothing to do with Vampires, the only similarity being is that low Dharma Kuei-Jin needing to drink blood. By then though Kuei-Jin gain Chi from breathing in a humans breath at mid-tier and then gaining it ambiently at a higher tier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:09:37-07:00","id":1387480,"title":"","content":"Dude if you are undead and drink blood and die from sunlight how can you say they have nothing to do with Vampires with a straight face?<br /> <br /> I don't remember the Gehenna book talking about Caine being a Yama King, but let me run with that idea, since lately I've found inspiration in embracing ideas I wouldn't initially go for. So in this case we can have Caine in the mantle of the Dark Father or Ebon Dragon and that kind of works as being a Yama King, or maybe Renegade Yama King or Hell loyal Yama King. So maybe Caine eventually asked for forgiveness but it wasn't that simple and he has to earn it.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and there are apocryphal 2nd gen beyond Zillah, Enosh and Irad. We have the Nameless and King and Queen the story of Haquim says he slew and self embraced from. We have the Typhon who embraced Osiris, but Osiris very much could be just 4th gen. We also have the Crone who Caine Staked and left to die, and well I am pressing X to doubt she died in the sun.<br /> <br /> We also have the theory of Azazel Caine, where Caine and Lilith had to work together to make the 2nd gen. Maybe they made a set for Lilith as well. Maybe Wan Gui are Lilith's tribe and the Cainites are Caines, and there is overlap?<br /> <br /> So we have room for early Caitiffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:44:13-07:00","id":1387491,"title":"","content":"1) Kuei-Jin flesh rot off in the sunlight while Kindred just burn when in contact with it<br /> <br /> 2) Kuei-Jin only need blood at the very early stages of being one, with later on they never have to do so again<br /> <br /> 3) The Kuei-Jin are direct descendants of the Wan Xian. The group of supernatural fighters dedicated to solely fighting the Yama Kings and other supernatural malign entities. Even if you go with the niche of Caine being a Yama King, it falls flat because A) Caine was a human in the beginning while the Yama Kings were always supernatural Wardens of Hell created by the August Personage of Jade and B) when he finally became a Vampire (the first one), he only sired a limited amount of childer while the Kuei-Jin literally were the Wan Xian cursed with undeath all at once. All 10,000 of them. Not only that more Kuei-Jin after the original batch of cursed ones from the Wan Xian are only created from a ghost going back to their body after escaping the Thousand Hells. No where does it say any of Caine's childer were brought about in this way. And again early Caitiffs aren't possible in the beginning of Kindred prehistory because there is such an already limited scope of Vampires- they would definitely know who sired them directly.<br /> <br /> Even if we broach your Lilith theory, those Caitiffs would've been enemies of the Wan Xian because they fought against malign entities at all costs. They couldn't possibly be the childer of Lilith because she didn't sire 10,000 people and we already have conflicts on whether she was a Mage, Vampire, or the &quot;Queen&quot; of Monsters, or the baby mama of Lucifer apparently. Its best to throw her out of the window when knitting up any theories because she's so contradictory and many writers in White Wolf just keep hamfisting her in many stories because &quot;kewl XDDD she was Adam's first real wife, not Eve! Mysterious!?!?&quot; Looking at all these holes, its pretty conducive to infer the Kuei-Jin aren't vampires at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T08:55:16-07:00","id":1387508,"title":"","content":"No, I said Gehenna thinks you can SUPPOSE Caine as a Yama King, just an IDEA for ST, nothing more, don\u2019t think too much<br /> <br /> And well, I always think anyone who looks close to KotE should know Wan Gui are not vampire at all<br /> <br /> The origin of Wan Gui is much closer to Risen of Wraith than Kindred, but in general they\u2019re crossover creature:<br /> 1. Have spiritual ties like Garou<br /> 2. Have ghost ties like Wraith<br /> 3. Have a system like Kindred<br /> <br /> It also shows how powerful Wan Xian are<br /> <br /> They just like the whole KotE, which has a very big cross, all sorts of supernaturals are thrown into a melting pot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:22:07-07:00","id":1387511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1387491#post1387491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Kuei-Jin flesh rot off in the sunlight while Kindred just burn when in contact with it<br /> <br /> 2) Kuei-Jin only need blood at the very early stages of being one, with later on they never have to do so again<br /> <br /> 3) The Kuei-Jin are direct descendants of the Wan Xian. The group of supernatural fighters dedicated to solely fighting the Yama Kings and other supernatural malign entities. Even if you go with the niche of Caine being a Yama King, it falls flat because A) Caine was a human in the beginning while the Yama Kings were always supernatural Wardens of Hell created by the August Personage of Jade and B) when he finally became a Vampire (the first one), he only sired a limited amount of childer while the Kuei-Jin literally were the Wan Xian cursed with undeath all at once. All 10,000 of them. Not only that more Kuei-Jin after the original batch of cursed ones from the Wan Xian are only created from a ghost going back to their body after escaping the Thousand Hells. No where does it say any of Caine's childer were brought about in this way. And again early Caitiffs aren't possible in the beginning of Kindred prehistory because there is such an already limited scope of Vampires- they would definitely know who sired them directly.<br /> <br /> Even if we broach your Lilith theory, those Caitiffs would've been enemies of the Wan Xian because they fought against malign entities at all costs. They couldn't possibly be the childer of Lilith because she didn't sire 10,000 people and we already have conflicts on whether she was a Mage, Vampire, or the &quot;Queen&quot; of Monsters, or the baby mama of Lucifer apparently. Its best to throw her out of the window when knitting up any theories because she's so contradictory and many writers in White Wolf just keep hamfisting her in many stories because &quot;kewl XDDD she was Adam's first real wife, not Eve! Mysterious!?!?&quot; Looking at all these holes, its pretty conducive to infer the Kuei-Jin aren't vampires at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude you are confusing Vampire with Cainite. Wan Gui and Cainites are both vampires. If their were say cursed humans who turned into wolves and manwolves they would be werewolves just like garou are werewolves just not the same kind of werewolf.<br /> <br /> They are vampires, just not the same kind. Were does it say you have to burn in the sunlight to be a vampire, in the Dracula Novel he just lost his powers.<br /> <br /> And very few of the Wan Gui were Wan Xian, only the first generation of them were. The Wan Gui only bear the cursed legacy, which in my opinion a lot wouldn't view themselves as having any connection to the Wan Xian since they were rando humans and not demigods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:31:04-07:00","id":1387515,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#212529\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <b>Definition of <i>vampire</i></b><br /><br /> <br /> </span><br /> </span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#212529\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:Open Sans\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:Open Sans\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:Open Sans\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">1</span></span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#303336\"><span style=\"font-family:Open Sans\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:Open Sans\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>: </b>the reanimated body of a dead person believed to come from the grave at night and suck the blood of persons asleep</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Open Sans,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/vampire</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> I don't see anywhere that says Vampires have to disintegrate in sunlight to be a vampire, or that you can't be Asian. By this Reasoning Dracula from the Novel isn't a vampire, but Blade Vampires are.<br /> <br /> And what about Necromancers who learn how to subsist off of ghostly essence, are they now no longer vampires?<br /> <br /> Chinese legends of vampires have stories of them shapeshifting into tigers and stealing your chi out of your mouth or butthole.. Even high Dharma Vampires who can drink breath still can drink blood and many still indulge, just as some still eat flesh. Meanwhile we had Salubri who learned to subsist off of miniscule amounts of breath lifeforce from everyone in a crowd, so they stopped being vampires?</span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:40:57-07:00","id":1387519,"title":"","content":"Kuei-Jin are their own class of supernatural. The only similarity they bare is Sunlight damage and needing to drink blood (which is only the case of low Dharma Kuei). Like Rock113 just said, their basically a cross of many splats from a meta perspective rolled into one. I also don't know why you mean the Dracula Novel because the Vampires in this oWoD are apparently entirely based on Caine and the Abrahamic God (which is another topic I discuss incessantly about on other threads) - to be a Vampire in oWoD is pretty clear, your sire and sire after that and after has to descend from Caine. If not, your not a Vampire. The ONLY Vampire clan that is 100% confirmed that has nothing to do with Caine is the Nagaraja, who were Warlocks under the service of Caine guarding Enoch who did a ritual who became Vampires. Beside that one faction thats really it.<br /> <br /> Even with you mentioning only the first generation of Kuei-Jin were related to the Wan Xian doesn't dispel what I've stated before- the Kuei-Jin don't have any relation to Caine whatsoever. They are created from completely different metaphysics, have different abilities, don't have sires at all, have different Yin and Yang states depending on their aspected view etc. Even the &quot;dark&quot; counterpart of the Kuei-Jin is nothing like Beast Kindred have. The P'o of a Kuei is actually intelligent like how a Shadow of a Wraith/Risen would be and can actually monologue instead the characters head i.e speak. Not to even mention the Dharma outlooks, which is alot to go into itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 05-11-2020, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:44:34-07:00","id":1387523,"title":"","content":"You are missing entirely the point of the discussion. Vampire isn't a scientific term like Homo Sapien Sapien. All Cainites are Vampires. Not all Vampires are Cainites. I'm dipping out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:50:27-07:00","id":1387526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites#post1210691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, follow me on this, it's a bit of a trip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just going to re-quote it here, but the thread is about a page down;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386183-v20-peach-making-kuei-jin-into-kindred#post1386183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much what the topic title says.<br /> <br /> Since the odds of getting a proper KotE20 seem rather slim and to make my next campaign run smoother I\u2019m looking at turning the Kindred of the East into Cainite vampires. I\u2019m also hoping that bringing them into line with the rest of the Kindred it will smooth out some of the unfortunate implications of making all the Oriental undead a separate species.<br /> <br /> In universe, the notion that Kuei-jin are a separate species of supernatural is a combination of propaganda (from both sides) and sincere confusion due to the Eastern Kindred descending from an unrecorded Antediluvian rather than being a bloodline of one the known western thirteen.<br /> <br /> In this case, I\u2019m running with the notion that there were just 13 Antediluvians is a translation error; the actual translation of the Book of Nod is \u201cand their numbers were 3 by 10\u201d (as was suggested in a footnote in the book of the same name) and not \u201c3 and 10.\u201d<br /> <br /> The 13 known Antediluvians were just those who found each other after the Flood and sired progeny while others either died in the battle with the Second Generation, never came out of torpor after the flood or chose to use being scattering by the flood/presumed dead to strike out on their own unnoticed... one of these latter ones became the ancestor of the Kindred of the East.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I figure as a clan their culture falls mostly into line with the fluff of Kindred of the East (i.e. they organize into various courts just as their brethren gather in cities under a prince). They have an utter disdain for embracing (though their Beast has other ideas) and view their ghouls as their half-damned children (i.e. KotE Dhampyrs are actually either ghouls or, in some cases, Revenants).<br /> <br /> The Dharma are Paths of Enlightenment, albeit ones that retain the virtues of Conscience (Hun), Self-Control (Yin) and Courage (Yang) with their Beast (P\u2019o) opposing their Humanity/Path rating. Their bearings improve social actions just as high Humanity does.<br /> <br /> Their Clan weakness is a particularly cunning Beast that seizes control whenever they fail a Conscience roll; basically a separate personality in line with the P\u2019o natures. It is while in this state that they will Embrace with abandon; the idea that the wicked spontaneously arise as Kuei-Jin is a lie they convince themselves of to absolve themselves of the guilt of having damned another soul to unlife because they lost control of their P\u2019o.<br /> <br /> Their clan disciplines are Blood Sorcery (representing their control over Chi... the Path of Blood\u2019s \u2018Theft of Vitae\u2019 is where legends that the Elders can feed off the breath of mortals arises), Vicissitude (representing the various shintai; blood, flesh, bone, etc.) and Auspex (representing the Soul Arts that typically revolve around perception of and influence over the soul).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:24:49-07:00","id":1387537,"title":"","content":"I know it\u2019s off topic but I also have questions about the origin of Wan Gui: What\u2019s their relations with Wan Xian? The first generation of Wan Gui are obviously Wan Xian, but later ones? <br /> <br /> People who die with great sin will reborn in Hell and only those having strong willpower can flee to the Earth successfully and become Wan Gui. What\u2019s their relations with Wan Xian, anyway? <br /> <br /> To be honest I see nothing, are these mortals all reincarnation of original Wan Xian who suffer the curse of Karmic? Or anything else?<br /> <br /> Their children, dhampry, are also said to be the reincarnation of Wan Xian\u2019s childer, Golden Children: All dhampry are the reincarnation of killed Jin Hai, Scarlett Queen uses them to remind Wan Gui of their greatest sin. <br /> <br /> But... in theory a Yang-imbalanced Wan Gui can reproduce dhampry as many as he can, and this seems to have nothing to do with how many golden children his ancestor Wan Xian (if it\u2019s right) had reproduced? <br /> <br /> Maybe how many dhampry a wan gui can reproduce is decided by karmic at the beginning, maybe. For example, a Wan Xian killed his three golden children and was cursed, so his reincarnated Wan Gui may only reproduce three dhampry at most...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-11-2020, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:52:25-07:00","id":1387558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1387519#post1387519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kuei-Jin are their own class of supernatural. The only similarity they bare is Sunlight damage and needing to drink blood (which is only the case of low Dharma Kuei). Like Rock113 just said, their basically a cross of many splats from a meta perspective rolled into one. I also don't know why you mean the Dracula Novel because the Vampires in this oWoD are apparently entirely based on Caine and the Abrahamic God (which is another topic I discuss incessantly about on other threads) - to be a Vampire in oWoD is pretty clear, your sire and sire after that and after has to descend from Caine. If not, your not a Vampire. The ONLY Vampire clan that is 100% confirmed that has nothing to do with Caine is the Nagaraja, who were Warlocks under the service of Caine guarding Enoch who did a ritual who became Vampires. Beside that one faction thats really it.<br /> <br /> Even with you mentioning only the first generation of Kuei-Jin were related to the Wan Xian doesn't dispel what I've stated before- the Kuei-Jin don't have any relation to Caine whatsoever. They are created from completely different metaphysics, have different abilities, don't have sires at all, have different Yin and Yang states depending on their aspected view etc. Even the &quot;dark&quot; counterpart of the Kuei-Jin is nothing like Beast Kindred have. The P'o of a Kuei is actually intelligent like how a Shadow of a Wraith/Risen would be and can actually monologue instead the characters head i.e speak. Not to even mention the Dharma outlooks, which is alot to go into itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they're literally called Kindred of the East and the KotE books routinely refer to them as vampires many times over. Hell, just looking at the introductory part of Kindred of the East it specifically calls them vampires almost twenty times on page 10 alone. Whether you like it or not or agree with the book or not, Wan Kuei are considered a type of vampire. All you're doing is arguing, &quot;The book is wrong and the authors are using that term in a way I don't like!&quot; so okay, yeah, your opinion is noted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T13:21:39-07:00","id":1387579,"title":"","content":"Best guess? They'll declare that whatever the kuejin version of gehenna was, happened.<br /> <br /> They'll also de-emphasize the kuejin by talking about all the cainites who survived by learning to avoid them, and even learned how to use them as a sort of shield to protect themselves from rival vampires.<br /> <br /> And now that the kuejin are extinct, all the cainites who were using them as de facto shields are scrambling to deal with both the good and bad results of this. On the good side, they have much more territory now. On the bad side, western cainites are now trickling in and trying to take over. The cainites of the east are really missing the kuejin, who were never all that numerous due to the excruciatingly slow method of their reproduction. The cainites of the east loved that these overrated, small in number, slow to reproduce, easy to avoid creatures inspired such terror from their western brethren. The kuejin were the boogeymen who protected the eastern cainites from western cainite invasion.<br /> <br /> Now that's over, and war is commencing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T13:52:55-07:00","id":1387585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1387537#post1387537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it\u2019s off topic but I also have questions about the origin of Wan Gui: What\u2019s their relations with Wan Xian? The first generation of Wan Gui are obviously Wan Xian, but later ones?<br /> <br /> People who die with great sin will reborn in Hell and only those having strong willpower can flee to the Earth successfully and become Wan Gui. What\u2019s their relations with Wan Xian, anyway?<br /> <br /> To be honest I see nothing, are these mortals all reincarnation of original Wan Xian who suffer the curse of Karmic? Or anything else?<br /> <br /> Their children, dhampry, are also said to be the reincarnation of Wan Xian\u2019s childer, Golden Children: All dhampry are the reincarnation of killed Jin Hai, Scarlett Queen uses them to remind Wan Gui of their greatest sin.<br /> <br /> But... in theory a Yang-imbalanced Wan Gui can reproduce dhampry as many as he can, and this seems to have nothing to do with how many golden children his ancestor Wan Xian (if it\u2019s right) had reproduced?<br /> <br /> Maybe how many dhampry a wan gui can reproduce is decided by karmic at the beginning, maybe. For example, a Wan Xian killed his three golden children and was cursed, so his reincarnated Wan Gui may only reproduce three dhampry at most...</div> </div> </div> </div>There generations of Wan Xian before the ones that fell to corruption and became the Wan Kuei. There was a metaphysical/mystical system that replenished their number with brave and righteous souls. Then corruption happened and the August Personage in Jade saw this, cursed them, and redirected the system to take the souls of sinful and corrupt making more Wan Kuei to suffer the curse and hopefully achieve redemption.<br /> <br /> I am fuzzy on the reincarnated golden children though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T15:24:28-07:00","id":1387819,"title":"","content":"I think a lot would have to be scrapped in order to make it work, but I think it would be a worthwhile (and possibly a lot less racist) way of bringing them back for V5.<br /> <br /> Potentially the biggest issue would be that their understanding of their own origins might just be wrong. I have no problem with this at all, reckoning as I do that there's a lot of room for the Caine origin story given for western vampires being a myth.<br /> <br /> I also love the idea, introduced in the &quot;Chronicles of the Black Labyrinth&quot; book, that the Garou Nation are mistaken and that Beast-of-War, Eater-of-Souls, and the Defiler Wyrm are the only real Triat, but that's another thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T10:09:58-07:00","id":1388708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1387585#post1387585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am fuzzy on the reincarnated golden children though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is another mess<br /> <br /> It is said that Wan Gui will see their sins on Dhamprys, meaning Wan Gui have some biological or reincarnation connections with original Wan Xian, but this opposes former one<br /> <br /> As you say, if the connection between Wan Xian and Wan Gui is just the system, why do Wan Gui see their \u201csin\u201d on DHAMPRY? They should have nothing to do with original Golden Children!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T11:00:56-07:00","id":1388712,"title":"","content":"Just being another pack of Cainites would strip the Hungry Dead of a lot of their appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T11:14:49-07:00","id":1388716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1388712#post1388712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just being another pack of Cainites would strip the Hungry Dead of a lot of their appeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but it might also mean they could be more involved in the game proper.<br /> <br /> Wan Kuei as is don't have much opportunity for visiting Elysium or hanging out at the Succubus Club. Not much point of having them be Kindred if you're not going to do a mixed game.<br /> <br /> It restricts them to being Ming Xiao and the monks you beat up for the sarcophagus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T11:44:50-07:00","id":1388722,"title":"","content":"That is part of why I would make the mechanics involving them simply (for the sake of brevity I suggest the VtR rules). And much of the separation is social, or mandated by the elders of each group. Which suggests narrative possibilities if the PCs are going off and hanging around with a bad crowd - i.e. the other group of vampires. And imagine the scandal if some Hungry Dead were admitted to Elysium, or Cainites into the proper courts of the Hungry Dead. The tension in the story differences should produce drama.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.engr.psu.edu/xiao/about.html\" target=\"_blank\">Edit: And i don't know what Professor Xiao has to do with anything. </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":".  a hopping vampire made me do it 05-15-2020, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T13:15:04-07:00","id":1388745,"title":"","content":"To tell the truth, I kind of like what they did in the BBC Dracula miniseries where sometimes the dead just rise hungry for the living for no apparent reason, and in certain cases exceptional examples can develop into vampires. That's more or less how it goes in Vampire: the Requiem, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T14:41:24-07:00","id":1388763,"title":"","content":"In VTR there main Clans have multiple &quot;nebulous&quot; (as in its basically what you want) for their exact origin IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T11:29:13-07:00","id":1389006,"title":"","content":"This is kind of were they came from in the first place. Not Cainites per se, as the Cain thing was possibly a myth and not reality, but they were just other clans that used the same rules presented in the core rules. See Clan Bushi in Dark Alliance Vancouver for example. Latter on when revised reset the game they developed the kindred of the east to be something else. now that they have rest the game once again we may see them go back to the Kindred of the east being just other clans who have a different progenitor than Cain. The is already hinted at in Chicago by Night.<br /> <br /> Just like Gehenna being potentially cyclical was presented in early editions Cain not being the progenitor of all vampires has a well, so I could easily see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T22:01:22-07:00","id":1389191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1210691-what-if-the-hungry-dead-are-just-cainites?p=1388712#post1388712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just being another pack of Cainites would strip the Hungry Dead of a lot of their appeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going back and rereading Transylvania Chronicles, it's funny to read what is presented Saulot's mesage to his Antedeluvian siblings - about how his motivation for millennia of villainy was simple jealousy over how the Kuei Jin were objectively so much cooler than the kind of undeath that Caine stuck his childer with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-17-2020, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}